<h1 class="article-title">Decisions Adopted by the Liepāja SEZ Board on 7 December</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority’s 2024 budget</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Board reviewed and approved the Authority’s budget for 2024: operating revenue of EUR 15,766,038, operating expenditure of EUR 12,460,072 and investment cash flow of EUR 2,777,339. The Board also approved the Authority’s budget forecast for the following five years.</p><p>The operating revenue forecast takes account of expected cargo throughput by stevedoring companies at the Port of Liepāja, the approved port charges for 2024 and expected income from property leases.</p><p>In 2024, the Liepāja SEZ Authority will continue work on three major development projects: reconstruction of the ferry berth (Berth 46), transformation of the former Liepājas metalurgs plant into the modern Liepāja Industrial Park, and development projects in the Port of Liepāja’s outer harbour.</p><p> </p><p>Implementation of investment projects</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Board reviewed and supported an investment project by Roechling Industrial Liepaja LSEZ Ltd totalling EUR 200,000. The company plans to purchase universal robotic arms and related equipment between 27 December 2023 and 31 December 2024. According to its declaration of</p><p>enterprise size, Roechling Industrial Liepaja LSEZ Ltd is a medium-sized enterprise and the maximum permitted aid intensity for these investments is 50%.</p><p> </p><p>In 2023, the Liepāja SEZ Authority concluded 15 investment agreements with SEZ companies, with a total planned investment of EUR 5,481,903.28.</p><p> </p><p>Disposal of real estate</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Board considered and agreed to the disposal of the land plot at 1 Laboratorijas Street in Liepāja because the property is not needed for the Authority’s functions.</p><p> </p><p>Real estate lease and building rights agreements</p><ul><li>On 31 January 2023, the Liepāja SEZ Authority and BaltEx Bulk Ltd signed an agreement granting building rights for the land plot at 5 Pulvera Street in Liepāja, within the SEZ, to prepare a preliminary construction design for a cargo storage area.</li></ul><p>The Board examined documents submitted by BaltEx Bulk Ltd and noted that changes in market and geopolitical circumstances have affected cargo types, requiring amendments and additions to the cargo categories and corresponding changes to the preliminary construction design.</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Board decided to conclude an agreement with BaltEx Bulk Ltd extending the reservation agreement until 31 July 2024.</p><p> </p><ul><li>The Board also decided to amend the lease agreement concluded on 5 March 1998 between the Liepāja SEZ Authority and NORPLAST PIEMARE LSEZ JSC for properties at 7 Kaiju Street and 37 Atslēdznieku Street in the Port of Liepāja.</li></ul><p>The Board approved NORPLAST PIEMARE LSEZ JSC’s request to separate the part of the property at 37 Atslēdznieku Street from the original lease and conclude a separate lease agreement for it.</p><p> </p><ul><li>On 3 April 2019, the Liepāja SEZ Authority and EB Liepājā Ltd concluded an agreement granting building rights for the property at 11 Zemgales Street in Liepāja to implement the construction project for a new production building and reconstruction of two buildings at that address.</li></ul><p>The Liepāja SEZ Board reviewed and approved the leasing of the newly built production facility and office building to Golden Fields Factory LV Ltd.</p></div>
